{"name":"Rapunzel","hex":"#f6d77f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Rapunzel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A German fairy tale about a girl imprisoned in a tower who lets down her long hair for a rescuer to climb.","The fictional girl who is the protagonist and title character of the fairy tale."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Rapunzel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rapunzel","blocks":[{"text":"\"Rapunzel\" is a German fairy tale most notably recorded by the Brothers Grimm and published in 1812 as part of Children's and Household Tales. The Grimms' story was developed from the French literary fairy tale of Persinette by Charlotte-Rose de Caumont de La Force (1698), which itself is an alternative version of the Italian fairy tale Petrosinella by Giambattista Basile (1634)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Rapunzel-Paul-Hey.jpg/330px-Rapunzel-Paul-Hey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rapunzel"},{"title":"Rapunzel (Tangled)","blocks":[{"text":"Rapunzel is a fictional character in Disney Animation's Tangled (2010). Based on the title character from the Brothers Grimm fairy tale of the same name, Rapunzel is a young princess kept unaware of her royal lineage by Mother Gothel, a vain woman who kidnaps her as a baby to hoard her hair's healing powers and remain young forever. A song is needed to activate the healing powers. Raised in a secluded tower, Rapunzel escapes with a wanted thief, Eugene \"Flynn Rider\" Fitzherbert, who promises to help her see the elusive floating lights in time for her 18th birthday, in exchange for a crown she has hidden from him. She is voiced by actress and singer Mandy Moore."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/6a/Rapunzel_tangled.png/330px-Rapunzel_tangled.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rapunzel_(Tangled)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Johnny_Gruelle_illustration_-_Rapunzel_-_Project_Gutenberg_etext_11027.jpg/500px-Johnny_Gruelle_illustration_-_Rapunzel_-_Project_Gutenberg_etext_11027.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Johnny_Gruelle_illustration_-_Rapunzel_-_Project_Gutenberg_etext_11027.jpg/500px-Johnny_Gruelle_illustration_-_Rapunzel_-_Project_Gutenberg_etext_11027.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Illustration by Johnny Gruelle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJohnny_Gruelle_illustration_-_Rapunzel_-_Project_Gutenberg_etext_11027.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Dresden_Altmarkt_14.jpg/500px-Dresden_Altmarkt_14.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Dresden_Altmarkt_14.jpg/1280px-Dresden_Altmarkt_14.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Dresden_Altmarkt_14.jpg/500px-Dresden_Altmarkt_14.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rapunzel in Dresden, Saxony, Germany","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADresden_Altmarkt_14.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Early_poems_of_William_Morris_-_Florence_Harrison_illustration_at_page_091.png/500px-Early_poems_of_William_Morris_-_Florence_Harrison_illustration_at_page_091.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Early_poems_of_William_Morris_-_Florence_Harrison_illustration_at_page_091.png/1280px-Early_poems_of_William_Morris_-_Florence_Harrison_illustration_at